phi-adapter-sdk (0.11.0-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * ChannelDataType::Json and sendChannelObjectStateUpdated(): a composite
    channel value, for the kinds whose meaning does not fit in one number. A
    firmware update is a status and two versions, and reporting only one of
    them loses the other two.
  * The value is a flat set of named scalars, serialized by the SDK. Not a
    general escape hatch: the shape cannot break the envelope it travels in,
    and a projection field has to name a scalar anyway.
  * channelProjectionField(kind) names the one field that carries a composite
    value's scalar meaning - `status` for DeviceSoftwareUpdate. Everything that
    reduces a value to one comparable thing (a history row, an automation
    condition) reads it from there, so the adapter, the rules and the history
    cannot disagree about what the channel is.
  * Colour keeps its own type and its own transport; it predates this and has
    no scalar meaning to project.

 -- Marius Schumacher <marius.schumacher@phisys.com>  Mon, 08 Sep 2026 12:45:00 +0200

